1. WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS

Hina (the program, the local server, the interface, the original personas,
and the texts and documentation that come with the program) is owned by
Project H.I.N.A. This license transfers no ownership: it only allows the use
described below.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

You may download, install and use Hina free of charge on your own computers,
for personal, non-commercial use.

"Non-commercial use" means not using Hina as part of a product or service that
is sold, rented or provided to others.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Without written permission from Project H.I.N.A., you may not:

a) copy Hina beyond what is needed to install and use it;
b) redistribute, sell, rent, lend, sublicense or make Hina available to
   others, including by download or inside another package;
c) modify, translate or create derivative works of Hina;
d) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble Hina, except to the extent the
   applicable law expressly allows it despite this restriction;
e) remove or change copyright, trademark or license notices;
f) use Hina to break the law or the terms of the services you connect to it.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Hina includes third-party components, each under its own license, listed in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and with the full texts in the "licenses" folder of the
installed program. This license does not apply to those components and does
not restrict any right their licenses give you. In particular, the libraries
under the LGPL stay as separate files inside the program, and you may replace
them with modified versions, as that license allows.

5. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES AND YOUR KEYS

Hina works with API keys that you obtain from and pay directly to the
providers (for example Google, Groq, ElevenLabs, Deepgram). Your use of those
services is governed by each provider's terms. What Hina sends to them is
described in the privacy policy:
https://github.com/Project-H-I-N-A/hina-releases/blob/main/PRIVACY.en.md

6. ACTIONS ON YOUR COMPUTER

With the agent on, Hina can read and write files, run commands and operate
programs on your computer. Actions that write, delete or run something ask for
your confirmation unless you tick "always allow". You are responsible for what
you authorize.

7. NO WARRANTY

Hina is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
including warranties of operation, fitness for a particular purpose or absence
of errors, to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law.

8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Project H.I.N.A. is not
liable for indirect damages, data loss, lost profits or service provider
charges arising from the use of Hina. Nothing in this license removes
consumer rights that the law guarantees and that cannot be waived.

9. END OF THE LICENSE

This license ends automatically if you break any of its terms. In that case
you must stop using Hina and delete the copies you have.

10. EARLIER VERSIONS

Versions distributed before this license under the GNU GPL version 3 remain
governed by it for those who received them. This license applies from the
version in which it appears.

11. CHANGES

Changes to this license are published with the Hina version that brings them
and apply to that version onward.

